        {
          "id": "excessive-oil-consumption-is-the-hidden-problem",
          "title": "Excessive oil consumption is the hidden problem",
          "description": "Unlike smoke or noises, it often goes unnoticed until it's too late. In our 24,650 quote dataset, we identified three primary causes:",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "cards",
              "cards": [
                {
                  "title": "Valve stem seals - 40% of cases",
                  "text": "Oil leaks past worn seals when the engine is off. Consumption often 1L per 1,000 miles. Repair: £500-£1,500.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Valve stem seals - 40% of cases Oil leaks past worn seals when the engine is off. Consumption often 1L per 1,000 miles. Repair: £500-£1,500."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Piston rings - 45% of cases",
                  "text": "Worn rings allow oil past the pistons during combustion. Consumption often 1L per 500 miles or less. Repair: £1,500-£4,000+.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Piston rings - 45% of cases Worn rings allow oil past the pistons during combustion. Consumption often 1L per 500 miles or less. Repair: £1,500-£4,000+."
                },
                {
                  "title": "PCV system - 10% of cases",
                  "text": "Faulty positive crankcase ventilation. Repair: £100-£200.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "PCV system - 10% of cases Faulty positive crankcase ventilation. Repair: £100-£200."
                },
                {
                  "title": "Turbo seals - 5% of cases",
                  "text": "Oil passing through turbo bearings. Repair: £450-£3,000+.",
                  "highlight": "",
                  "meta": "",
                  "icon": "",
                  "items": [],
                  "fullText": "Turbo seals - 5% of cases Oil passing through turbo bearings. Repair: £450-£3,000+."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "The critical rule: Any oil consumption of 1L per 1,000 miles or more requires investigation. The consequences of ignoring it are catastrophic - bearing damage, catalytic converter failure, and engine seizure."
            },
            {
              "type": "label",
              "text": "Common affected vehicles & engines"
            }
          ],
          "links": [],
          "source": {
            "sectionId": "excessive-oil-consumption-is-the-hidden-problem",
            "order": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "follow-this-decision-tree-to-identify-the-cause",
          "title": "Follow this decision tree to identify the cause",
          "description": "EXCESSIVE OIL CONSUMPTION │ ├─── Measure consumption (L per 1,000 miles) │ │ │ ├── < 0.5L → Normal → Monitor monthly │ │ │ ├── 0.5-1.0L → Monitor closely → Check every 1,000 miles │ │ │ └── > 1.0L → Get diagnosis → Book diagnostic │ ├─── Is there blue smoke? │ │ │ ├── On cold start → Valve seals → Valve seal replacement │ │ │ ├── On acceleration → Piston rings → Piston ring replacement │ │ │ └── Constant → Turbo seals → Turbo repair │ └─── Check PCV system │ ├── Faulty → Replace PCV → £100-£200 │ └── OK → Internal engine issue → Engine replacement",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "label",
